<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Basic Multisection Webpage</title>
    <style>
        * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; color: #333; }
        
        header { background: #f1f1f1; padding: 20px; text-align: center; }
        header h1 { color: #333; }
        
        nav ul { 
            list-style: none; background: #333; display: flex; 
            justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; 
        }
        nav li a { 
            display: block; color: #f1f1f1; padding: 14px 20px; 
            text-decoration: none; 
        }
        nav li a:hover { background: #ddd; color: #000; }
        
        .flex-container { display: flex; flex-direction: row; }
        .flex-container > div { margin: 10px; padding: 20px; flex: 1; min-width: 250px; }
        
        section { min-height: 400px; padding: 40px 20px; text-align: center; }
        #section1 { background: #e3f2fd; }
        #section2 { background: #f3e5f5; }
        #section3 { background: #e8f5e8; }
        
        footer { background: #f1f1f1; padding: 20px; text-align: center; }
        
        @media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
            .flex-container { flex-direction: column; }
            nav ul { flex-direction: column; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>My Multisection Site</h1>
        <p>Welcome to a basic responsive webpage with multiple sections.</p>
    </header>
    
    <nav>
        <ul class="topnav">
            <li><a href="#section1">Home</a></li>
            <li><a href="#section2">About</a></li>
            <li><a href="#section3">Services</a></li>
            <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
    
    <main class="flex-container">
        <div id="section1">
            <h2>Section 1: Introduction</h2>
            <p>This is the first content section. It uses flexbox for layout and adapts to screen size.[web:12][page:0]</p>
        </div>
        <div id="section2">
            <h2>Section 2: Features</h2>
            <p>Key features include responsive design, navigation, and distinct sections for better organization.[web:13][page:1]</p>
        </div>
        <div id="section3">
            <h2>Section 3: Content</h2>
            <p>Additional content goes here. Customize colors, add images, or extend with JavaScript.</p>
        </div>
    </main>
    
    <footer id="contact">
        <p>&copy; 2026 Basic Webpage. Built with HTML & CSS.</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
